 about\nhealth impacts and how ozone pollution forms in Colorado, visit:\nhttps://cdphe.colorado.gov/ozone-pollution-and-your-health\n\nHEALTH INFORMATION...Increasing likelihood of respiratory symptoms\nand breathing discomfort in active children and adults and people\nwith lung disease, such as asthma. Active children and adults, and\npeople with lung disease, such as asthma, should reduce prolonged\nor heavy outdoor exertion.","ends":"2026-08-22T16:00:00-06:00","severity":"Unknown","areaDesc":"Adams, CO; Broomfield, CO; Weld, CO; Denver, CO; Larimer, CO; Douglas, CO; Jefferson, CO; Boulder, CO; Arapahoe, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.2e1856bd470a3808e6319b390c73b6c01dea1650.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.2e1856bd470a3808e6319b390c73b6c01dea1650.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-08-22T11:55:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KBOU 221155 AFDBOU Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Denver/Boulder CO 555 AM MDT Sat Aug 22 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Heat eases, along with an increase in shower and storm coverage this weekend. - Highest coverage of showers and storms expected today, along with a few severe storms on the plains this afternoon and evening and then again Sunday. - Gradual drying next week","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=BOU&issuedby=BOU&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-08-22T08:46:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION...Today and tonight... An uptick in storm coverage is expected this afternoon and evening as moisture increases across the region, with scattered wetting rains and strong to severe wind gusts expected with storms. With the increasing moisture will come improvements to relative humidity values despite another day of above normal temperatures. RH is expected to remain above critical thre","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=BOU&issuedby=BOU&product=FWF&format=CI"},"coagmet":{"station_id":"ftl01","station_name":"Fo